@event know_grisk_collectors
# en: Running Late
title [359088] = 逾期了
# en: {x} is counting coins on the common-room table, and coming up short. {They} borrowed from Grisk in the village to get through the month, and the payment was due on Friday. "He was so nice about it," {x} says. "He called me his friend. He'll give me another week, surely."
text [f2adcf] = {x}在公共休息室的桌上数硬币，怎么数都不够。{they}为了熬过这个月，向村里的格里斯克借了钱，星期五就该还了。“他人可好了，”{x}说，“还叫我朋友。他肯定会再宽限我一个星期的。”
# en: A common room at night, a student counting a few coins on a table and coming up short, a friend watching from the doorway.
scene [f4eb0e] = 夜里的公共休息室，一个学生在桌上数着几枚硬币，怎么数都不够，一个朋友在门口看着。
# en: "Ask him for more time, then."
opt.left.label [8449b2] = “那就去求他宽限几天吧。”
# en: {x} goes down to the village to ask. The next evening there are two large, polite visitors at the castle gate asking for {x} by name, and {x} spends a fortnight's supper money making them go away. Nobody hears {x} call Grisk a friend after that.
opt.left.say.1 [be9e81] = {x}下山去村里求情。第二天傍晚，城堡大门口来了两位块头很大、彬彬有礼的访客，指名要找{x}；{x}花掉了两个星期的晚饭钱才把他们打发走。从那以后，再没人听见{x}管格里斯克叫朋友。
# en: "Pay him tonight. Trust me."
opt.right.label [bb34b8] = “今晚就还他。相信我。”
# en: You tell {x} about the waistcoats, and the trolls inside them, and how polite and thorough they are. {x} goes pale, and you lend {x.them} the rest. Grisk takes the coins at the Newt that night with real regret. "Such a pity," he says. "They were looking forward to it."
opt.right.say.1 [363e6b] = 你给{x}讲了那两件马甲，马甲里的巨魔，还有他们有多客气、多彻底。{x}脸都白了，你把差的钱借给了{x.them}。当晚格里斯克在蝾螈酒馆收下硬币，看上去真心遗憾。“太可惜了，”他说，“他们可期待了。”

@event know_grisk_newt
# en: Paid in Advance
title [e9d7a4] = 预付
# en: A stationer's in the village is selling a whole term of ink, paper and candles at half price, paid in advance. Half the castle is queuing down the lane. It's a real bargain, as long as the shop is still there at the end of term.
text [94e8ad] = 村里一家文具店在半价预售一整个学期的墨水、纸和蜡烛。半个城堡的人都在巷子里排队。这确实划算，只要学期末这家店还在。
# en: A village lane, a long queue of students outside a small shop with a hand-painted sign in the window offering half price.
scene [fb2af1] = 村里的小巷，一家小店门外排着长长的学生队伍，橱窗里挂着手绘的半价招牌。
# en: Buy a term's worth
opt.buy.label [4c28d4] = 买一学期的量
# en: Three weeks later the shutters are down and there's a notice on the door about creditors. Half the castle stands in the lane reading it. So do you.
opt.buy.say.1 [b7be27] = 三个星期后，店门的卷帘拉下了，门上贴着一张关于债主的告示。半个城堡的人站在巷子里读它。你也在其中。
# en: The shop lasts the term, just. You don't buy ink again until spring, and feel very clever every time you don't.
opt.buy.say.2 [53c8b7] = 那家店勉强撑过了这个学期。直到开春你都没再买过墨水，每次不用买，你都觉得自己特别聪明。
# en: Walk past the queue
opt.pass.label [1cdab8] = 从队伍旁走过
# en: You walk past. You'll never know whether it was a bargain. That bothers you more than it should.
opt.pass.say.1 [8668e9] = 你走了过去。你永远不会知道那到底划不划算。这件事比它应该的更让你耿耿于怀。
# en: Ask Grisk at the Newt first
opt.ask.label [e915ee] = 先去蝾螈酒馆问问格里斯克
# en: You buy Grisk a drink at his corner table and mention the shop. He sighs at the ceiling like a man discussing rain. "Three weeks," he says. "Four, if the landlord is sentimental." It's gone in three, and you were not in the queue.
opt.ask.say.1 [d3fabd] = 你在格里斯克的角落桌请他喝了一杯，提起那家店。他对着天花板叹了口气，像在谈论下雨。“三个星期，”他说，“房东心软的话，四个。”三个星期后店就没了，而你没有排那个队。

@event know_grisk_favours
# en: Just a Small Favour
title [e6ac78] = 只是帮个小忙
# en: {x} looks relieved, which worries you. Grisk has offered to forget {x.their} whole debt for one small favour: carrying a parcel across the village after dark, for a client he didn't name. "It's nothing," {x} says. "It's a parcel. What's in a parcel?"
text [4650db] = {x}看上去松了一口气，这让你担心。格里斯克提出，只要帮一个小忙，就把{x.their}债一笔勾销：天黑后替一位他没说名字的客人把一个包裹送过村子。“没什么的，”{x}说，“就是个包裹。包裹里能有什么？”
# en: A castle stairwell, a relieved-looking student holding a small parcel wrapped in oilcloth, a friend frowning at it.
scene [aec74c] = 城堡的楼梯间，一个如释重负的学生抱着一个油布包着的小包裹，一个朋友皱眉看着它。
# en: "A parcel's a parcel."
opt.left.label [351231] = “包裹就是包裹。”
# en: {x} carries the parcel, and the debt is gone, just like that. {They} won't tell you where {they} took it, and for the rest of term {they} won't go down to the village alone.
opt.left.say.1 [33d6fa] = {x}送了包裹，债就这么没了。{they}不肯告诉你送去了哪儿，而且这学期剩下的日子里，{they}再也不肯一个人下山去村里。
# en: "Pay in coin. I'll help."
opt.right.label [11950e] = “用钱还。我帮你。”
# en: You know about Grisk's favours, and the clients he never names. You and {x} scrape the coins together between you instead. Grisk takes them with a little bow. "Prudent," he says, and sounds almost disappointed.
opt.right.say.1 [9a76a4] = 你知道格里斯克的那些“小忙”，还有他从不说名字的客人。于是你和{x}一起凑齐了钱。格里斯克微微鞠了一躬收下。“明智，”他说，听上去几乎有点失望。

@event know_amaranth_book
# en: Peppermint and a Charm
title [29b8fc] = 薄荷和一道咒语
# en: {x} has had a cold for a week and has cured it, {they} say{s}, with a remedy of {x.their} own: peppermint, honey, a pinch of something from the alchemy lab and a charm {they} won't explain. It works. {They} {are} too embarrassed to show anyone. "Amaranth would laugh," {they} say{s}.
text [1864dd] = {x}感冒了一个星期，据{they}说，是用{x.their}自己的方子治好的：薄荷、蜂蜜、从炼金实验室弄来的一小撮什么东西，再加一道{they}不肯解释的咒语。真的管用。{they}不好意思给任何人看。“阿玛兰斯会笑话我的，”{they}说。
# en: A dormitory window seat in winter, a student holding a steaming mug of something green, a friend sniffing it doubtfully.
scene [1ad9c5] = 冬天宿舍的窗边座位，一个学生捧着一杯冒着热气的绿色东西，一个朋友满腹狐疑地闻了闻。
# en: Ask for a cup yourself
opt.left.label [8eeac3] = 自己也讨一杯
# en: {x} makes you a cup. It's dreadful, and it works. {They} make{s} you promise to tell no one, and you never do, which seems a pity.
opt.left.say.1 [82a25a] = {x}给你冲了一杯。难喝极了，但管用。{they}让你保证谁也不告诉，你也真的从没说过，想想挺可惜的。
# en: "She keeps a book of these."
opt.right.label [9ff1b9] = “她有一本专门记这个的簿子。”
# en: You tell {x} about Sister Amaranth's book of her students' remedies. It takes a week of persuading. When {x} finally shows her, Amaranth tries it, says nothing at all, and copies it out on a fresh page in her square hand. {x} doesn't stop smiling for a day.
opt.right.say.1 [effaf3] = 你告诉{x}，阿玛兰斯修女有一本簿子，专门抄录学生们的方子。你劝了一个星期。{x}终于拿给她看时，阿玛兰斯尝了尝，一句话也没说，用她方正的字迹把它抄在了新的一页上。{x}笑了一整天。

@event know_amaranth_rounds
# en: Who Comes at Night
title [4db2d9] = 夜里谁会来
# en: {x} is in the infirmary overnight with a fever, and frightened, the way people are when they're ill and it's getting dark. "What if something happens," {they} say{s}, "and nobody comes?" Visiting hours are nearly over.
text [5a794f] = {x}发着烧，要在医务室过夜，而且很害怕，人生病、天又黑下来的时候就会这样。“万一出了什么事，”{they}说，“却没人来怎么办？”探视时间快结束了。
# en: An infirmary ward at dusk, a feverish student in a bed by the window, a friend on the chair beside it, the lamps being lit.
scene [9da953] = 黄昏时的医务室病房，一个发烧的学生躺在窗边的床上，一个朋友坐在床边的椅子上，灯正一盏盏点亮。
# en: Stay until they send you out
opt.left.label [526b43] = 一直待到被赶出去
# en: You stay, talking about nothing, until you're sent out with a scolding. {x} is asleep by then. You aren't, for hours.
opt.left.say.1 [db2576] = 你留下来，东拉西扯，直到挨了一顿训被赶出去。那时{x}已经睡着了。而你几个小时都没睡着。
# en: "She does every round herself."
opt.right.label [1acad4] = “每一轮查房都是她亲自来。”
# en: You tell {x} about the rounds: every bed, every night, by Amaranth herself, and never once missed. {x} doesn't quite believe you. In the morning {they} tell{s} you {they} woke at two, and there she was with her lamp. "She nodded at me," {they} say{s}, amazed.
opt.right.say.1 [4d273b] = 你给{x}讲了查房的事：每一张床，每一个晚上，都是阿玛兰斯亲自来，从没漏过一次。{x}不太相信。第二天早上{they}告诉你，{they}两点醒来，她果然提着灯在那儿。“她还冲我点了点头，”{they}惊奇地说。

@event know_pell_not_yet
# en: Not Yet
title [033adc] = 还不行
# en: Pell is restocking the bottom of the wall when you come in, and his oldest drawer is open beside him, the one with the yellowed card in it. He looks at you over the drawer for longer than usual, as if measuring something twice.
text [e88357] = 你进门时，佩尔正在给墙最底下补货，他最老的那个抽屉在他身边开着，就是放着那张发黄卡片的那个。他隔着抽屉看了你比平时更久，像是在把什么东西量第二遍。
# en: An apothecary's wall of a thousand small drawers, one very old drawer open near the floor, an old man kneeling beside it with a yellowed card.
scene [bd211c] = 药铺里一整面墙的上千个小抽屉，靠近地面的一个很老的抽屉开着，一位老人跪在旁边，拿着一张发黄的卡片。
# en: Wait for him to finish
opt.left.label [2fc371] = 等他忙完
# en: He finishes, shuts the drawer and serves you as if nothing happened, counting aloud, as always. On your way out you notice he's watching you go.
opt.left.say.1 [0c7669] = 他忙完了，关上抽屉，像什么都没发生过一样招呼你，照旧大声数着。出门时你发现他一直看着你走。
# en: Ask about the card
opt.right.label [ec7472] = 问问那张卡片
# en: You ask about the card, the draught "of your own strength". Pell takes it out, reads it, and looks at you again. Then he puts it back, and under "Not yet." he adds one word in his precise hand: "Nearly." He doesn't explain. He doesn't need to.
opt.right.say.1 [84ca5a] = 你问起那张卡片，那剂“以己之力”的药。佩尔把它拿出来读了一遍，又看了看你。然后他把它放回去，在“还不行。”下面用他工整的字迹添了一个词：“快了。”他没有解释。他也不需要解释。

@event know_vey_own_face
# en: It Slides Off
title [16a343] = 它滑掉了
# en: {x} has been trying all week to glamour {x.their} roommate's hair green, for a dare, and it won't hold: it slides off within the hour, every time. {They} {are} about ready to give up on illusion altogether.
text [730c92] = 为了一个赌，{x}一整个星期都在想用幻术把{x.their}室友的头发变绿，可就是撑不住：每次不到一个小时就滑掉了。{they}差不多准备彻底放弃幻术了。
# en: A dormitory mirror, a frustrated student pointing a wand at a roommate's hair, which is flickering between two colours.
scene [fac88b] = 宿舍的镜子前，一个懊恼的学生拿魔杖指着室友的头发，那头发在两种颜色之间闪个不停。
# en: Practise with {x.them} all evening
opt.left.label [5784eb] = 陪{x.them}练一整晚
# en: You practise all evening. By midnight the green holds for two whole hours. {x} says that's progress, and goes to bed looking like someone who doesn't believe it.
opt.left.say.1 [dbe15a] = 你们练了一整晚。到午夜，那抹绿色撑了整整两个小时。{x}说这算进步，上床时却是一副不信的样子。
# en: "Try it on your own face first."
opt.right.label [f6c5fe] = “先在你自己脸上试试。”
# en: You tell {x} what Vey says: a glamour you can't hold on yourself won't hold on anyone. {x} tries it on {x.their} own nose, swears at the mirror for an hour, and then it holds. The roommate is green for a week. Vey hears of it, awards nobody any points, and smiles.
opt.right.say.1 [14ccff] = 你把维伊的话告诉{x}：自己身上都撑不住的幻术，放到谁身上也撑不住。{x}在{x.their}自己的鼻子上试，对着镜子骂了一个小时，然后就撑住了。室友绿了一个星期。维伊听说后，谁也没加分，只是笑了。

@event know_marisol_margins
# en: The Book in the Margins
title [542b1c] = 页边里的书
# en: {x} has the tidecalling textbook open at the same page {they} had last week, and the week before. "It makes sense when I read it," {they} say{s}, "and no sense at all in the lake." The exam is close. {They} {are} starting to talk about dropping the course.
text [dc7b05] = {x}的潮汐术课本翻开在上周、上上周的同一页。“读的时候明明都懂，”{they}说，“一下湖就全不懂了。”考试快到了。{they}开始说要退掉这门课。
# en: A library table, a student staring at the same open page of a tidecalling textbook, a friend sitting down across from them.
scene [1b837e] = 图书馆的桌边，一个学生盯着潮汐术课本的同一页，一个朋友在对面坐下。
# en: Drill {x.them} at dawn
opt.left.label [5b3c23] = 黎明时陪{x.them}练
# en: You spend three cold dawns at the lake with {x}, going through it line by line. It helps, a little. {x} passes narrowly, and is grateful, and still hates the book.
opt.left.say.1 [03c8cf] = 你陪{x}在湖边过了三个寒冷的黎明，一行一行地过。有点帮助。{x}勉强及格了，心怀感激，但还是讨厌那本书。
# en: "Ask Marisol about her poems."
opt.right.label [54da73] = “去问问玛丽索尔她的诗集。”
# en: You tell {x} about the book of poems Marisol wrote her own tidecalling into as a student. {x} asks her, mortified. Marisol lends it on the spot, dripping. The margins make sense of everything. {x} passes well, and says the poems were awful but the margins were wonderful.
opt.right.say.1 [0d6706] = 你告诉{x}，玛丽索尔当学生时把自己的潮汐术写在了一本诗集的页边。{x}窘得要命地去问她。玛丽索尔浑身滴着水，当场就把书借了出来。页边的笔记让一切都说得通了。{x}考得很好，说那些诗糟透了，但页边棒极了。

@event know_mabel_tins
# en: A Tin on the Barge
title [3181a2] = 驳船上的一只铁罐
# en: {x} has gone quiet this month. {They} {are} homesick, though {they} would never say so. A letter from home came on Tuesday, and it's still unopened beside {x.their} plate.
text [c7d504] = {x}这个月变得很安静。{they}想家了，虽然{they}绝不会说出口。星期二家里来了一封信，现在还没拆，就放在{x.their}盘子旁边。
# en: A refectory table at supper, a quiet student with an unopened letter beside the plate, a friend sliding onto the bench next to them.
scene [24ad8b] = 晚饭时膳堂的桌边，一个沉默的学生盘子旁放着一封没拆的信，一个朋友挪到旁边的长凳上坐下。
# en: Sit with {x.them} at supper
opt.left.label [0ec4df] = 晚饭时陪{x.them}坐着
# en: You sit with {x} at supper every night that week and talk about nothing much. It doesn't fix anything. On Sunday {they} open{s} the letter, with you there.
opt.left.say.1 [b7ca94] = 那个星期你每天晚饭都陪{x}坐着，随便聊些什么。这什么也解决不了。星期天，{they}当着你的面拆开了那封信。
# en: Write to Mabel
opt.right.label [5ac6ac] = 给梅布尔写信
# en: You send a note down to Mabel in the village. Two days later a tin comes up on the barge, addressed to {x} in round handwriting: tea, a slab of cake, and no note. {x} never finds out who sent it, and keeps the tin on {x.their} windowsill all year.
opt.right.say.1 [1f2a64] = 你给村里的梅布尔捎了张字条。两天后，驳船送来一只铁罐，圆圆的字迹写着{x}的名字：里面是茶、一大块蛋糕，没有字条。{x}始终不知道是谁寄的，那只铁罐在{x.their}窗台上放了一整年。

@event know_mabel_fourth_cake
# en: A Cake With a Name
title [b102ea] = 有名字的蛋糕
# en: It's {x}'s birthday, and you've brought {x.them} to Mabel's, because there's nowhere better. {x} looks at the three cakes on the counter as if choosing between them were the hardest decision of the year.
text [5d819e] = 今天是{x}的生日，你带{x.them}来了梅布尔茶馆，因为没有更好的地方了。{x}看着柜台上的三块蛋糕，仿佛在它们之间挑一块是今年最难的决定。
# en: A village tea shop, three cakes under glass domes on the counter, two students leaning over them, a woman in an apron watching.
scene [ea669f] = 村里的茶馆，柜台上三块蛋糕罩在玻璃罩里，两个学生俯身看着，一个系围裙的女人在一旁看着他们。
# en: Let {x.them} choose
opt.left.label [93f23b] = 让{x.them}自己挑
# en: {x} chooses the lemon after ten minutes, and says it was the right choice, and then eats half of yours.
opt.left.say.1 [df1461] = 十分钟后{x}选了柠檬的，说这是正确的选择，然后吃掉了你的一半。
# en: Ask Mabel for a fourth cake
opt.right.label [a78873] = 问梅布尔要第四种蛋糕
# en: You ask, quietly, whether there's a fourth. Mabel looks at {x}, vanishes into the back and comes out with something pink and alarming. She writes its card while you watch: {x}'s name, and the date. {x} eats it, survives, and is very proud to be on the card.
opt.right.say.1 [a6722d] = 你悄悄问有没有第四种。梅布尔看了看{x}，消失在后厨，端出来一样粉红色、看着叫人心惊的东西。她当着你的面写好卡片：{x}的名字，还有日期。{x}吃了，活了下来，并且为上了那张卡片而非常骄傲。

@event know_isolde_mercy
# en: A Witness to Character
title [0a6753] = 品格证人
# en: {x} has been sent to the headmistress over a prank that went further than {they} meant, and has asked you along as a witness to {x.their} good character. Headmistress Marrow hears all of it without a word. Then she turns to you.
text [6416c5] = {x}因为一个闹过了头的恶作剧被送到院长那里，请你一起去，为{x.their}品格作证。马罗院长一言不发地听完了全部经过。然后她转向你。
# en: A tall tower study, a headmistress behind her desk with her hands folded, two students standing before it, one of them very pale.
scene [56a706] = 高塔里的书房，院长双手交叠坐在桌后，两个学生站在桌前，其中一个脸色煞白。
# en: Vouch for {x.them}, warmly
opt.left.label [d7e1f9] = 热情地为{x.them}担保
# en: You vouch for {x}, warmly and at length. The headmistress thanks you, and gives {x} a month of detentions anyway. "Character," she says, "is what one has left after the detention."
opt.left.say.1 [e8ec1b] = 你热情洋溢地为{x}担保了好半天。院长谢过你，照样罚了{x}一个月的禁闭。“品格，”她说，“是禁闭之后剩下的东西。”
# en: Wait for her question
opt.right.label [02c130] = 等她发问
# en: You say nothing, and wait. Sure enough, she asks what you think would be just. You tell her honestly: not nothing, but less than a month, and the damage put right by {x}'s own hands. She considers it, and, to {x}'s astonishment, she listens.
opt.right.say.1 [1c27d0] = 你什么也没说，只是等着。果然，她问你觉得怎样才算公正。你老实告诉她：不是不罚，但不到一个月，而且损坏的东西要{x}亲手修好。她想了想，而让{x}大吃一惊的是，她听进去了。

@event know_grimsby_upper_floor
# en: Out of Print
title [64df47] = 绝版
# en: You need a book for an essay: the one every reading list cites and nobody has seen in thirty years. The library's copy went missing before you arrived. Grimsby, asked, gives you a book about lighthouses instead and says it's the next best thing. He may even be right.
text [47ab6c] = 你写论文需要一本书：每份书单都引用、却三十年没人见过的那本。图书馆那本在你入学前就丢了。你去问格林斯比，他给了你一本关于灯塔的书，说这是退而求其次的最佳选择。他说不定还真说对了。
# en: A crowded bookshop, an old bookseller holding out a book about lighthouses, a student behind the counter's ladder looking upward.
scene [d80181] = 拥挤的书店里，一位老书商递出一本关于灯塔的书，一个学生站在柜台后的梯子旁抬头往上看。
# en: Take the lighthouse book
opt.left.label [f88d9c] = 拿那本灯塔书
# en: You read the lighthouse book. There's a chapter on lenses that turns out, absurdly, to help with your essay. It's still not the book, and Grimsby is unbearable about it.
opt.left.say.1 [d44ccb] = 你读了那本灯塔书。里面有一章讲透镜，荒唐的是，它居然对你的论文有帮助。但它还是不是那本书，而格林斯比为此得意得叫人受不了。
# en: Climb to the upper floor
opt.right.label [e65a5a] = 爬上楼上那层
# en: You climb the ladder behind the shop, skipping the third and fourth rungs, and spend an hour in the dust among the remainders. The book is there, under a stack of almanacs. Grimsby, below, says he had no idea, and charges you half price for knowing about the ladder.
opt.right.say.1 [685272] = 你爬上店后面的梯子，跳过第三和第四级，在滞销书的灰尘里待了一个小时。那本书就在那儿，压在一摞年鉴下面。格林斯比在底下说他完全不知道，然后因为你知道那架梯子，只收了你半价。

@event know_grimsby_parcels
# en: On Credit
title [28a515] = 赊账
# en: {x} has been avoiding the village for a month. It comes out eventually: Grimsby posted {x.them} three books on credit, exactly the right ones, and {they} can't pay, and {they} {are} too ashamed to walk past the shop. "He'll have my name on a list," {they} say{s}.
text [427dec] = {x}一个月都在躲着村子。最后还是说出来了：格林斯比赊账给{x.them}寄了三本书，恰好都是{they}需要的，可{they}付不起，羞得连那家店门口都不敢走。“他肯定把我的名字记在单子上了，”{they}说。
# en: A castle corridor window looking down toward the village, a student turning away from it, a friend catching their sleeve.
scene [45b2c9] = 城堡走廊的窗户俯瞰着村子，一个学生转身背对窗户，一个朋友拉住了对方的袖子。
# en: Help {x.them} save up
opt.left.label [0e5740] = 帮{x.them}攒钱
# en: You help {x} put coins aside, week by week. It takes the rest of term. When {x} finally goes in to pay, Grimsby looks puzzled: he'd forgotten. {x} hadn't, for a single day.
opt.left.say.1 [97e1a8] = 你帮{x}一周一周地攒钱。这花了整个学期剩下的时间。{x}终于进店去还钱时，格林斯比一脸困惑：他早忘了。而{x}一天也没忘过。
# en: "He's never chased a debt."
opt.right.label [7f98c4] = “他从来不催债。”
# en: You tell {x} that Grimsby posts books on credit and has never chased a debt in his life. {x} goes down that afternoon to say sorry, and comes back with a fourth book and a cup of tea inside {x.them}. "He said to pay when I can," {they} say{s}, "and to stop being silly."
opt.right.say.1 [b86d30] = 你告诉{x}，格林斯比常赊账寄书，这辈子从没催过一笔债。{x}当天下午就下山去道歉，回来时多了第四本书，肚子里还多了一杯茶。“他说等我有钱再付，”{they}说，“还叫我别犯傻。”

@event know_ilse_frost
# en: Frost on the Inside
title [8bbca7] = 结在里面的霜
# en: Winter has got into the dormitories. The windows frost over on the inside every night, and the warming ward the professors put up keeps cracking. Everyone is sleeping in their coats, and the porters say it will be mended next week, as they said last week.
text [0e26f5] = 冬天钻进了宿舍。每天夜里窗户都从里面结霜，教授们布下的取暖结界一再开裂。大家都穿着大衣睡觉，门房说下星期就修好，上星期他们也是这么说的。
# en: A dormitory corridor in deep winter, windows frosted over on the inside, students in coats and hats, a girl in white furs looking unimpressed at a cracked ward.
scene [f3ea25] = 深冬的宿舍走廊，窗户从里面结满了霜，学生们穿着大衣戴着帽子，一个裹着白色毛皮的女孩不以为然地看着一道裂开的结界。
# en: Patch the ward with the others
opt.left.label [c87c72] = 和大家一起修补结界
# en: You and half the corridor patch it, badly, out of a textbook. It holds most nights. You get very good at sleeping in a hat.
opt.left.say.1 [071e26] = 你和半条走廊的人照着课本把它补上了，补得很糟。大多数夜里它还撑得住。你练就了戴着帽子睡觉的好本事。
# en: Ask Ilse
opt.right.label [0a147f] = 去找伊尔泽
# en: You go to Ilse, who knows Northern frost-craft better than anything the professors teach. She looks at the ward for less than a minute, says something rude about it in Northern, and reworks it with two fingers. The windows are clear by morning. She refuses all thanks, and accepts a scarf.
opt.right.say.1 [4d41df] = 你去找伊尔泽，她对北境霜术的了解胜过教授们教的任何东西。她看了那道结界不到一分钟，用北境话说了句难听的，用两根手指把它重新编了一遍。到早上窗户就干净了。她拒绝了所有道谢，却收下了一条围巾。

@event know_tamsin_backdrop
# en: A Forest by Post
title [604d28] = 寄来的森林
# en: The first-years' end-of-term play needs a backdrop, a forest at night, and you, somehow, have been volunteered to paint it. You have a week, a bucket of grey and no idea at all.
text [888980] = 一年级生的期末戏需要一块背景幕，画夜晚的森林，而不知怎么的，你被“自愿”去画它了。你有一个星期、一桶灰颜料，以及毫无头绪。
# en: A hall stage after supper, a huge blank canvas propped against the wall, a student with a bucket of grey paint and a letter full of sketches.
scene [14314f] = 晚饭后礼堂的舞台上，一大块空白画布靠在墙边，一个学生提着一桶灰颜料，手里拿着一封画满速写的信。
# en: Paint the best forest you can
opt.left.label [7f3232] = 尽力画一片森林
# en: You paint a forest. It looks like a forest from the back of the hall, if the lamps are low. The first-years are very kind about it.
opt.left.say.1 [06721a] = 你画了一片森林。从礼堂最后排看，灯光暗一点的话，它像一片森林。一年级生们对此非常宽容。
# en: Write to Tamsin for help
opt.right.label [741f5f] = 写信向塔姆辛求助
# en: You write to Tamsin, who learned illusion painting their grandmother's backdrops. The reply is six pages of sketches and insults about your brushwork. You follow it to the letter. On the night, the forest stirs in a wind that isn't there, and the hall gasps. You send Tamsin the programme.
opt.right.say.1 [bb7db7] = 你写信给塔姆辛，TA是给祖母画背景幕学会幻术的。回信是六页速写，外加对你笔法的各种挖苦。你一字不差地照做。演出那晚，森林在一阵并不存在的风里摇曳，整个礼堂都倒吸了一口气。你把节目单寄给了塔姆辛。
